invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_verify
reason: the host verifier reads an X for R whatever the affine conversion
  answers, so it compares r with what the conversion wrote for the point
  at infinity. The conversion writes zero there and r is not zero, so
  every test passes. The proof's stub of the conversion writes any
  bytes, and the proof requires the verdict 0 when it reports
  infinity.

--- old
    if (p256_wide_point_affine(x, NULL, &result) == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
--- new
    (void)p256_wide_point_affine(x, NULL, &result);
